# agent_harness

The `agent_harness` CLI (npm: @taowaonline/agent-harness) is a vendor-neutral
control plane for AI-assisted development: stable stage names (format, lint,
typecheck, test-unit, test-integration, eval-smoke, eval-full, security) that
map to language-specific tools via harness.toml profiles.

## When this rule applies

- The project has a `harness.toml`, or the user asks to set up / audit local
  CI, offline AI evals, or security posture for an AI project.

## What to do

- Discover commands, never guess: `agent_harness list`, then
  `agent_harness run <stage> --dry-run` to preview argv.
- Before proposing changes: `agent_harness validate`.
- After changes touching AI behavior (prompts, models, tools, retrieval):
  `agent_harness eval smoke --offline` minimum; release candidates run
  `agent_harness run release-check`.
- `skipped` is not `passed` — report the skip reason.
- Offline evals are the default; online only on explicit request.

## Reference

Full skill: SKILL.md in the installed package. Docs: architecture,
